                        "entry_id": "61bfe98d-a7f3-3aab-8edb-8d0feec89e51",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The quality of being adaptable; a quality that renders adaptable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "82a4ec1c-ba1a-4045-98b7-cfc015677a83",
                                "sense_id": "5a03b465-db01-3fae-bd6a-aa87538f7c8f",
                                "text": "But the real test of my adaptability came senior year, when I became chapter president of DKA."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "96fc7e80-2139-3770-ab04-8eccf64738aa",
                        "entry_id": "61bfe98d-a7f3-3aab-8edb-8d0feec89e51",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Variability in respect to, or under the influence of, external conditions; susceptibility of an organism to that variation whereby it becomes suited to or fitted for its conditions of environment; the capacity of an organism to be modified by circumstances."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7f1f7dd-86d8-4c78-9492-1bf1cde802c5",
                                "sense_id": "96fc7e80-2139-3770-ab04-8eccf64738aa",
                                "text": "Typically, tarantulas are either terrestrial or arboreal, but the Chilobrachys natanicharum can live in both enivronments^([sic]), the researchers said, demonstrating its adaptability."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
